  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing approval",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'that's a policy i could get behind', implying the user identifies with or imagines themselves endorsing the policy being referenced. This projection is indirect but inferred through the meme's structure, where the user is invited to adopt the persona of the approving figure (Bill Clinton) and the tone of the text. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the meme's humor and irony create a shared frame where the viewer is positioned as the one who could 'get behind' the policy, thus projecting themselves onto the textual endorsement.",
